#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
booking - agent-native CLI for Booking.com hotels, Taiwan locale (zh-tw, TWD). No booking.

Zero dependencies (Python 3.8+ stdlib). Every command supports --json and
returns the {ok, data|error} envelope used by the other ~/Projects CLIs.
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 api, 2 usage, 3 auth, 4 net/blocked.

Endpoints, measured 2026-10-30 with real requests (CDP Network capture on a
background tab of the user's signed-in Edge, then replayed with plain HTTPS)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Booking.com sits behind AWS WAF, on its HTML pages only. Plain HTTPS GET of a
page without cookies gets HTTP 202 + a 3.9 KB JS challenge (challenge.js,
awsWafCookieDomainList); with the `aws-waf-token` cookie that Edge holds it
answers 200. The GraphQL endpoint answered 200 with no cookie at all. The
bkng_sso_* cookies add the signed-in session (Genius prices, trips, wishlist).
So everything is plain HTTPS with the cookies copied from Edge (`booking
login`). On a WAF challenge the CLI takes Edge's current token (measured: a
session without the token got 202, then 200 after this step); if Edge's token
is the same, one background Edge tab loads the home page to pass the
challenge (that second step was not needed today, so it is unverified).
`--via browser` runs the same calls as fetch() inside a background tab (CDP
127.0.0.1:9222, Target.createTarget background=true).

  POST https://www.booking.com/dml/graphql?lang=zh-tw&selected_currency=TWD   (http)
       The site's own Apollo GraphQL. It accepts plain (non-persisted)
       queries, so the CLI sends its own small queries (field names taken
       from the site's FullSearchFragment / PropertyBlocks /
       PriceDisplayInfoIrene fragments in its JS):
       - AutoComplete: autoCompleteSuggestions(input:{prefixQuery,
         nbSuggestions}) -> destination {destId, destType, countryCode},
         displayInfo {title, subTitle, label}. 心齋橋 -> DISTRICT 2883.
       - search: searchQueries.search(input: SearchQueryInput) with
         location {searchString, destType, destId}, dates, nbRooms,
         nbAdults, nbChildren, childrenAges, pagination {rowsPerPage,
         offset}, sorters.selectedSorter (popularity / price /
         price_from_high_to_low / bayesian_review_score /
         distance_from_search), filters.selectedFilters "class=4;fc=2;
         mealplan=1" (= the URL's nflt). -> pagination.nbResultsTotal,
         searchMeta.geniusLevel, results[]: basicPropertyData (id, pageName,
         location.countryCode, starRating, reviews), displayName, location,
         showAdLabel + sponsoredListingData (ads), soldOutInfo, policies
         (showFreeCancellation, showNoPrepayment), blocks[] (blockId,
         finalPrice, freeCancellationUntil, onlyXLeftMessage,
         mealPlanIncluded), matchingUnitConfigurations (room names),
         priceDisplayInfoIrene: displayPrice.amountPerStay = the card's
         總金額 (stay total), chargesInfo 含稅費及其他費用 or 可能產生額外費用,
         excludedCharges (chargeInclusion EXCLUDED, chargeMode INCALCULABLE
         = e.g. Osaka accommodation tax not included), discounts (Genius).
         Measured: rowsPerPage 15/25/50 agree; 100 returned a different
         result set (2,309 instead of 65 hotels, other prices) -> 25 used.
         The site's price order is NOT monotonic (11,313 then 11,283;
         13,239 then 9,545 on the next page) -> price sorts read a pool and
         re-sort by total. Children change results: 心齋橋 3 adults 77
         hotels (SOLEIL 5,017), + child 7: 66 hotels (SOLEIL 5,574).
         Genius: same search anonymous vs signed in: 11322422 8,361 vs 7,051.
         destType HOTEL + destId <hotel id> returns that hotel first; its
         card was the hotel page's cheapest fitting rate for every hotel
         checked (9616998, 13963456, 11859964, 13935295).
         persuasion.autoextended = a hotel Booking adds from OUTSIDE the
         destination when few match (心齋橋 + 4-star + breakfast + free
         cancel: 4 in the district, 82 auto-extended up to 21 km away) ->
         dropped unless --include-nearby. Multi-room: Booking (and the site's
         own search) also lists one apartment that fits everyone for
         --rooms 2 (needsRoomsMatch=false, as the site sends it).
         showAdLabel / sponsoredListingData (the site's isAd): 0 seen in
         every search today; dropped when present.
       - wishlists: wishlistService.userWishlist -> wishlists[] (listId,
         name, nbHotels, hotels[] hotelId); saved add/rm:
         wishlistService.saveHotelToWishlistV2(input:{hotelId}) and
         removeHotelFromWishlistV2(input:{hotelId}) (mutation names from the
         site's JS), always followed by a re-read of userWishlist.
  GET  https://www.booking.com/hotel/<cc>/<pageName>.zh-tw.html?checkin=..&group_adults=..&group_children=..&age=..&no_rooms=..&selected_currency=TWD   (http, SSR, ~1.9 MB)
       ld+json Hotel (name, address, aggregateRating); JS var
       b_rooms_available_and_soldout[] (room b_id, b_name, b_blocks[]:
       b_block_id, b_raw_price = stay total for one room incl. taxes,
       b_stay_prices[b_stays=N] = total for N rooms, b_nr_stays = rooms left,
       b_max_persons, b_cancellation_type, b_mealplan_included_name,
       b_rate_is_genius, b_price_breakdown_simplified.b_charges_info_copy
       含稅費與其他費用 / b_excluded_charges_amount); the #hprt-table rows
       (tr data-block-id, data-fltrs occupancy_count.fit = the page's own
       "fits your party" flag, conditions: 免費取消 date / 不可退款 / 線上付款 /
       無需付款, beds); 入住時間 / 退房時間; 熱門設施.
       Measured: the page lists rates for 1..4 guests; only fit=1 rows fit
       3 adults + child 7. With no_rooms=2 the rows carry no fit flag; the
       page's suggested set is read from its markup (nr_rooms_<block>=N
       beside is_group_recommendation=1; that link is never requested).
  (whoami, same GraphQL endpoint)
       - whoami: personalProfile { ... on Profile { personalData {firstName,
         lastName} contactEmail {address} } } + geniusMembership (measured:
         GENIUS_LEVEL_2; without a session both answer 403 inside errors).
  GET  https://www.booking.com/index.zh-tw.html   (http, SSR)
       "csrfToken":"eyJ..." (24 h JWT) -> x-booking-csrf-token header for the
       wishlist mutations, as the site's own JS sends it.
  POST https://secure.booking.com/dml/graphql?lang=zh-tw   (http + session)
       UserTrips(first, filter {tripFilter: ACTIVE|PAST|CANCELLED}, sortBy)
       -> userTrips.edges[].node (id, title, startDate, endDate, stage,
       status, itemCount, bookedItemsCount). (UPCOMING/FUTURE are invalid.)
  GET  https://secure.booking.com/mytrips.zh-tw.html?tid=<trip id>&tab=bookings  (http + session, SSR)
       apollo store: singleTripTimeline.timelineGroups[].tripItems[]
       RESERVATION -> AccommodationReservation (hotelReservationId, start/
       endDateTime, reservationStatus, price, userPriceWeb, policy.name,
       numOfRooms, propertyData -> ReservationPropertyData name/city).
       Read-only; auth keys and confirmation URLs are never printed.

Price cards: a district search card can show a pricier flexible rate while a
cheaper rate exists (measured: 13963456 card 17,275 free cancellation, hotel
page cheapest fitting rate 15,548 non-refundable; the HOTEL-type search card
showed 15,548). `search --verify`, `hotel` and `price` show the cheapest.

Cookies / browser state: Booking keeps no locale/currency cookie; currency
is per request (selected_currency). Measured: Edge's own booking.com pages
show HKD by default and still did after this CLI's TWD tabs. Background tabs
set `bk_nav_search` (last search, 30 min); the browser path restores it to
what it was before the tab opened. Server-rotated session/consent cookies
(bkng, bkng_sso_auth_*, pcm_*) are left as the site sets them.

NEVER called: any booking, checkout, hold, payment or reservation path.
Unofficial. Undocumented, private API - it can break without warning.
